+### `maki.fn.transcript_anchors()` {#maki-fn-transcript_anchors}
+
+```lua
+maki.fn.transcript_anchors()
+```
+
+Read message anchors from the focused display transcript, oldest first.
+Each entry has `{message_index, role, preview, topline, height}`. Indexes
+and toplines are one-based. `message_index` addresses this display
+transcript, not the raw session log, and can be passed to `winrestview`.
+`preview` is the message's first line, truncated to 80 Unicode characters.
+`height` is the exact rendered segment height at the current width.
+
+Requires the `session_read` [plugin permission](#plugin-permissions).
+
+Requires the `session_read` [plugin permission](#plugin-permissions).
+
+**Returns:** (`table|nil`, `string|nil`) Array of anchor tables, or nil and an error.
+
+**Example:**
+
+```lua
+local anchors = maki.fn.transcript_anchors()
+for _, anchor in ipairs(anchors or {}) do
+  if anchor.role == "user" then print(anchor.preview) end
+end
+```
+
